      "text": "Heavy Rainfall Warning No. 9 #NCR_PRSD\nWeather System: Tropical Cyclone UWAN\nIssued at: 5:00 AM, 10 November 2025(Monday)\n\nORANGE WARNING LEVEL: Zambales, Bataan, Pampanga, Tarlac, Bulacan(Hagonoy, Paombong, Malolos, Calumpit, Pulilan, Plaridel, Baliuag, Bustos, San Rafael, San Ildefonso, San Miguel, Guiguinto, Bulakan, Bocaue, Balagtas, Pandi, Angat, Santa Maria) and Nueva Ecija(Cabiao, San Antonio, San Isidro, Gapan).\nASSOCIATED HAZARD: FLOODING is still THREATENING.\n\nYELLOW WARNING LEVEL: Rizal, Metro Manila, Cavite, Batangas, Laguna, Nueva Ecija(General Tinio, Aliaga, Bongabon, Cabanatuan, Carranglan, Cuyapo, Gabaldon, General Mamerto Natividad, Guimba, Jaen, Laur, Licab, Llanera, Lupao, Nampicuan, Palayan, Pantabangan, Penaranda, Quezon, Rizal, San Jose, San Leonardo, Santa Rosa, Santo Domingo, Munoz, Talavera, Talugtug, Zaragoza), Bulacan(San Jose del Monte, Dona Remedios Trinidad, Marilao, Norzagaray, Obando, Meycauayan) and Quezon(General Nakar, Infanta, Real, Mauban, Sampaloc, Lucban, Sariaya, Candelaria, Dolores, Tiaong, San Antonio, Tayabas, Lucena, Pagbilao, Panukulan, Burdeos, Polillo).\nASSOCIATED HAZARD: FLOODING in flood-prone areas.\nMeanwhile, light to moderate rains affecting Quezon(Agdangan, Alabat, Atimonan, Buenavista, Calauag, Catanauan, General Luna, Guinayangan, Gumaca, Jomalig, Lopez, Macalelon, Mulanay, Padre Burgos, Patnanungan, Perez, Pitogo, Plaridel, Quezon, San Andres, San Francisco, San Narciso, Tagkawayan, Unisan) which may persist within 3 hours.\nThe public and the Disaster Risk Reduction and Management Offices concerned are advised to MONITOR the weather condition and watch for the next warning to be issued at 8:00 AM today.\n\nFor more information and queries, please call telephone numbers 8927-1335 and 8927-2877 or log on to https://t.co/59mTpZJq1n.",
